ed\u2014edge represents empirical detection only."}, {"id": "rxn_012", "name": "Lightning (electrical discharge, N2-rich) route (empirical endpoint)", "inputs": ["mol_015", "mol_005", "mol_016", "mol_004"], "outputs": ["mol_012"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": ["Electric discharge"], "conditions": {"temperature": "300-355K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": true, "other": "Discharge in N2-buffered atmosphere, 7 days"}, "mechanism": "Spark discharge through reduced C/N atmosphere yields histidine empirically, via unspecified multistep radical/ionic chemistry.", "reasoning": "Empirical endpoint from Criado-Reyes et al. (2021), confirming histidine even when N2 is present and glass is absent. Mechanism unresolved."}, {"id": "rxn_013", "name": "UV/EUV irradiation of naphthalene/H2O/NH3 ice (empirical endpoint)", "inputs": ["mol_017", "mol_004", "mol_005"], "outputs": ["mol_012"], "environment": "Extraterrestrial", "agents": ["UV/EUV photons"], "conditions": {"temperature": "15K", "pressure": "<1e-9 atm (ultrahigh vacuum)", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": false, "other": "1:1:1 molecular ice, 4\u201320 eV photons, 4h irradiation, acid hydrolysis after extraction"}, "mechanism": "PAH/nitrogenous ice photochemistry creates residues that, upon acid hydrolysis, release histidine; stepwise intermediates unknown.", "reasoning": "Chen et al. (2008) direct endpoint evidence for His after ice irradiation + hydrolysis. Quantum yields reported; mechanism unresolved."}], "pathways": [{"pathway_id": "P1", "name": "Erythrose\u2013formamidine\u2013Strecker pathway (canonical, mechanistically resolved)", "description": "Formose chemistry generates erythrose from formaldehyde. Erythrose and formamidine condense (via Amadori-type chemistry) to give imidazole-4-glycol, which dehydrates to imidazole-4-acetaldehyde. The aldehyde undergoes Strecker reaction with ammonia and cyanide to yield histidine aminonitrile, which hydrolyzes to histidine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_007", "rxn_008"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_007", "mol_009", "mol_011"]}, {"pathway_id": "P2", "name": "Imidazole-4-glycol \u2192 imidazole-4-ethanol reduction\u2013oxidation branch", "description": "Imidazole-4-glycol reduces to imidazole-4-ethanol, which is then oxidized to imidazole-4-acetaldehyde before Strecker and hydrolysis to histidine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008", "mol_009"]}, {"pathway_id": "P3", "name": "Formamidine from HCN/NH3, with direct erythrose condensation and glycol\u2013ethanol dehydration", "description": "Formamidine from prebiotic HCN and ammonia is used in a network that leverages both direct condensation to imidazole-glycol and subsequent alternate dehydration paths.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_009", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_007", "mol_008", "mol_009", "mol_011"]}, {"pathway_id": "P4", "name": "Direct Fischer\u2013Tropsch-type catalysis (hydrothermal endpoint)", "description": "Hot mineral-catalyzed surface chemistry combines CO, H2, and NH3 directly to histidine through unresolved multistep transformation.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "name": "Electrochemical spark-discharge (Miller\u2013Urey) \u2013 CH\u2084/NH\u2083/H\u2082O/H\u2082 feedstocks", "description": "Electrical discharge through reduced C/N/H aqueous mixture generates histidine and other amino acids; mechanism unknown.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_011"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "name": "Electrochemical Miller\u2013Urey/N\u2082 route (CH\u2084/NH\u2083/N\u2082/H\u2082O input)", "description": "Lightning discharge includes added N\u2082, still yields histidine directly in endpoint analysis.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "name": "Phot