\": {\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.0,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.0,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.0\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.3,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 1.0,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.6,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.4,\n      \"feedback\": \"This pathway highlights direct formamidine formation from HCN/NH3, additional glycol chemistry, and then the canonical Strecker sequence. However, rxn_002, rxn_009, and rxn_008 are mass unbalanced. The chemical feasibility is thus not met in its present form; further, significant geochemical obstacles for formamidine accumulation apply, as emphasized in the literature. Mechanistic variants are appropriate, but only if the steps are properly balanced and justified.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_002\", \"rxn_009\", \"rxn_008\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Rebalance HCN/ammonia formamidine formation and glycol/ethanol branch reactions.\",\n        \"Clearly differentiate between experimentally observed versus only postulated sequence variants.\",\n        \"Annotate environmental or energy requirements for challenging steps.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.0\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.1,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 1.0,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.7,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.3,\n      \"feedback\": \"The Fischer\u2013Tropsch-type route recapitulates surface-catalytic CO/H2/NH3 chemistry, which has experimental support for endpoint His formation but no mechanistic detail. The drawn reaction is mass unbalanced (missing C, H, N, O), so cannot be accepted as valid as drawn. While the network properly presents this as a black-box empirical step, it must reflect atom/charge balance. Environmental representation (hyd