ied by Criado-Reyes et al. (2021), but the drawn reaction is mass unbalanced (see charge and atom balance). As with P5, this is an empirical endpoint route and must make that clear, but a reasonably balanced summary (even with 'byproducts') is needed for network validity.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_012 (missing 5C, O, N imbalanced \u2013 byproducts not included)\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Balance empirical endpoint conversion, reflecting true net reactants/products.\",\n        \"Note unresolved mechanism, but state literature yields/detection.\",\n        \"Consider referencing environment-specific details (pressure, pH, electrical configuration).\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.0\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.1,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 1.0,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.7,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.3,\n      \"feedback\": \"UV-irradiation of naphthalene/H2O/NH3 ice is supported as an empirical His-producing reaction (Chen et al., 2008), but the step as drawn is mass unbalanced. Pathway must be represented as an empirical endpoint (not mechanistic), with gross product balancing. Environment is well-justified (extraterrestrial, 15 K, UV/EUV).\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_013 (C, H, N, O mass discrepancies per check)\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Summarize as empirical endpoint route with balanced net reactants/products.\",\n        \"Note requirement for post-synthetic acid hydrolysis to release His.\",\n        \"Cite quantum yield and experimental detail.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.0,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.0,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.85,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.0\n      },\n      \"chemical_f