y\": 0.75,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.92,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.88,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.78,\n            \"feedback\": \"Direct condensation of erythrose and formamidine to imidazole-4-acetaldehyde, followed by Strecker sequence, is chemically plausible but only partially explored experimentally. Mechanistically, this shortcut is reasonable and pathway is more efficient, but rxn_006 (nitrile hydrolysis) remains unbalanced, which impacts achievability. All reactions except rxn_009 (balanceable) are unbalanced as written.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_006\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Fully balance condensation and hydrolysis reactions.\",\n                \"Confirm side product allocation for overall mass balance.\",\n                \"Reference any novel experimental support for direct condensation to aldehyde.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_011\": 0.85\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.85,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.95,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.9,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.83,\n            \"feedback\": \"Fischer\u2013Tropsch-catalytic hydrothermal route is an empirical endpoint pathway, directly supported by literature (Yoshino et al. 1971, Hayatsu et al. 1971). Mechanism is unresolved but direct production was demonstrated with CO/H2/NH3 on solid catalyst. The reaction is mass-balanceable (with coefficients). Environmental fit is excellent for hot mineral-catalytic setting. This remains an endpoint-only, non-sequenced approach.\",\n            \"approved\": true,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Clearly annotate that the mechanism is unresolved and this is a summary edge.\",\n                \"No change needed unless more explicit intermediates become available.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_012\": 0.65\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.65,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.65,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.95,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.8,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.73,\n            \"feedback\": \"CH4/NH3/H2/H2O spark discharge makes histidine (per Jiang et al. 2014; Criado-Reyes et al. 2021), but the endpoint route is mechanistically unresolved and rxn_012 is currently unbalanced as written. Environmental fit is strong. Appropriately represented as a one-step empirical summary.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_012\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Balance the empirical reaction as closely as possible.\",\n                \"Note empirical nature and unknown intermediates.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_013\": 0.65\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.65,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.65,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.95,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.8,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.73,\n            \"feedback\": \"Same as P6 but with HCN as C/N feedstock in empirical electrical discharge. Endpoint production is solidly literature-supported. Mechanism is unresolved and rxn_013 is unbalanced. Environmental setup is suitable.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_013\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Balance atoms in endpoint reaction.\",\n                \"Highlight this as an empirical summary.\"\n           